{"key":"enterprise/T1543.002","id":"T1543.002","name":"Systemd Service","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1543","tactics":["persistence","privilege-escalation"],"platforms":["Linux"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may create or modify systemd services to repeatedly execute malicious payloads as part of persistence. Systemd is a system and service manager commonly used for managing background daemon processes (also known as services) and other system resources. Systemd is the default initialization (init) system on many Linux distributions replacing legacy init systems, including SysVinit and Upstart, while remaining backwards compatible.…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1543/002","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--dfefe2ed-4389-4318-8762-f0272b350a1b","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.722Z","source_object_version":"1.6","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0060","name":"Service Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0060","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--5297a638-1382-4f0c-8472-0d21830bf705","page":"telem